# Heimdall action-type catalogue (sample for the demo action types).
#
# One "<action_type> consequential|informational" per line. Blank lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored; a type listed twice is refused. A hosting service
# loads this file with heimdall_workflow::ActionTypeCatalog::parse and gives the
# result to both the WorkflowEngine (with_catalog) and the DispatchActuator
# (with_catalog). A type not listed here cannot be proposed, and an empty
# catalogue refuses every proposal.
#
# The class is the deployment's decision, never the proposer's. Every execution
# needs a recorded human decision whatever the class: an informational action is
# acknowledged by a person before it runs, like any other.
#
# No running service hosts the Heimdall workflow engine yet; nothing in this
# compose stack reads this file today. [VLD-ANB-MIDGARD-0045]

cue-sensor consequential
dispatch-asset consequential
annotate-track informational
